IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lhl-dates`
IMPORT `lhl-rules`

-- Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (Vic) -- the questions of the HOST.
--
-- SEAT: the person or business that uses labour hire: the host to whom a provider supplies workers (s 3 "host"), and the
-- "client" of s 16 who proposes an arrangement for the supply of an individual to perform work. A sole trader, a farmer, a
-- small business owner, or the officer answering for a company. "Is this arrangement labour hire?", "May I enter into it
-- with this provider?", "Is it an avoidance arrangement I must not enter, and must I report it?", "Am I caught as someone
-- involved?", "Must the provider show me its licence?", "What is the most I can be ordered to pay, and until when?". The
-- Authority, inspectors and the courts get no seat. The provider's questions are in lhl-seat.l4, the worker's in
-- lhl-seat-worker.l4; the three draw on the same rules in lhl-rules.l4, so they cannot disagree about the law.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts and calls the rules of lhl-rules.l4. The s 16(3) duty to notify is a DEONTIC rule run
-- inside; no question takes a DEONTIC or an EVENT.
--
