§ `Labour hire licensing in Victoria: the host's questions`

§§ `Is it labour hire (ss 7 to 11)`

@export Is my arrangement with a business that supplies workers to me an arrangement for labour hire services under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (ss 7 to 10)? It is if, in a business, the provider supplies workers it pays to work for you; or a recruitment or placement business places workers with you whom you pay and also arranges their accommodation; or a contractor management business recruits independent contractors for you and manages their contracts. The regulations can add or exclude cases.
GIVEN `the provider's business` IS A `Kind of business` @desc The business the provider conducts: a business of providing recruitment or placement services; a business of providing contractor management services; another business; or no business
      `the arrangement is mainly` IS A `Character of the arrangement` @desc What your arrangement with the provider is, wholly or principally: the supply of labour to you; recruiting or placing individuals to perform labour for you; or something else
      `how the individuals are engaged` IS A `How the individuals are engaged` @desc How the individuals who do the work are engaged: a provider supplies them to others to perform work and must pay them for it; a provider recruits or places them with others (such as you) who must pay them; a provider recruits them as independent contractors for others and manages their contract performance; or none of these
      `the provider arranges their accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider procures or provides accommodation for the individuals for some or all of the time they do the work
      `the regulations take it to be labour hire` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Labour Hire Licensing Regulations prescribe circumstances that take this to be labour hire services (answer no if unsure)
      `the regulations exclude it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations exclude the provider, its services, or the individuals supplied or placed with you, from the Act (answer no if unsure)
      `the regulations exclude the individuals as workers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations exclude the individuals (or the services they provide) from being workers under the Act (answer no if unsure)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Is my arrangement for labour hire services` MEANS
    `ss 7 to 10 -- provides labour hire services` (`The arrangement` WITH
        `the kind of business` IS `the provider's business`
        `the character` IS `the arrangement is mainly`
        `the engagement` IS `how the individuals are engaged`
        `accommodation is procured or provided for the individuals` IS `the provider arranges their accommodation`
        `the regulations take it to be labour hire services` IS `the regulations take it to be labour hire`
        `the regulations exclude the provider, services or individuals` IS `the regulations exclude it`
        `the regulations exclude the individuals as workers` IS `the regulations exclude the individuals as workers`)

§§ `Using an unlicensed provider (ss 15, 16, 95)`

@export Am I forbidden to enter into this labour hire arrangement because the provider is unlicensed, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 15)? You must not enter into an arrangement for labour hire services unless the provider holds a licence in force, except where the provider was on the public Register as a licence holder when you entered into it, or you otherwise have a reasonable excuse. The maximum civil penalty is 800 penalty units for an individual and 3200 for a company.
GIVEN `it is for labour hire services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the arrangement is for the provision of labour hire services (the answer to the question on whether your arrangement is for labour hire services)
      `the provider holds a licence in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider holds a labour hire licence that is in force when you enter into the arrangement
      `the provider was on the Register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provider was shown on the Register of Licensed Labour Hire Providers as the holder of a licence when you entered into the arrangement
      `I have another reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you otherwise have a reasonable excuse for entering into the arrangement (a question for the court if disputed)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I forbidden to use this provider` MEANS
    `s 15 -- entering the arrangement is forbidden` `it is for labour hire services` `the provider holds a licence in force` `the provider was on the Register` `I have another reasonable excuse`

@export Am I forbidden to enter into an arrangement for the supply of a worker because it is meant to avoid the Act, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 16(2))? Where the supplier is not on the Register with a licence in force, you must not enter into the arrangement if you know, or have reasonable grounds to suspect, that it is meant to avoid or get around an obligation under the Act. The maximum civil penalty is 800 penalty units for an individual and 3200 for a company.
GIVEN `it is for the supply of an individual to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you propose to enter into an arrangement with another person (the supplier) for the supply of an individual to perform work, for you or someone else
      `the supplier is on the Register with a licence in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the supplier is shown on the Register of Licensed Labour Hire Providers as the holder of a licence in force when the arrangement is proposed
      `I know or suspect it is to avoid the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you know, or have reasonable grounds to suspect, that the arrangement is for the purpose of avoiding or getting around an obligation the Act would otherwise impose on you, the supplier or anyone else
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I forbidden to enter the avoidance arrangement` MEANS
    `s 16(2) -- entering the avoidance arrangement is forbidden` (`s 16(1) -- the section applies` `it is for the supply of an individual to work` `the supplier is on the Register with a licence in force`) `I know or suspect it is to avoid the Act`

@export Did I report a suspected avoidance arrangement to the Labour Hire Licensing Authority in time, or can I still, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 16(3))? Where the supplier is not on the Register with a licence in force, you must notify the Authority as soon as reasonably practicable after you become aware, or reasonably suspect, that the proposed arrangement is meant to avoid the Act. The maximum civil penalty is 200 penalty units for an individual and 800 for a company.
GIVEN `it is for the supply of an individual to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you propose to enter into an arrangement with another person (the supplier) for the supply of an individual to perform work
      `the supplier is on the Register with a licence in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the supplier is shown on the Register as the holder of a licence in force when the arrangement is proposed
      `I became aware or suspected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have become aware, or reasonably suspect, that the arrangement is for the purpose of avoiding or getting around an obligation under the Act
      `the day I became aware` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you became aware or began to suspect it (any day otherwise)
      `the days that were reasonably practicable` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after that it was reasonably practicable for you to notify the Authority (a judgment: 0 for the same day)
      `I have notified the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have notified the Authority
      `the day I notified it` IS A DATE @desc If so, the day you notified it (any day otherwise)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Whether I had to report`
`Did I report the avoidance arrangement in time` MEANS
    IF NOT `s 16(1) -- the section applies` `it is for the supply of an individual to work` `the supplier is on the Register with a licence in force`
    THEN `s 16 does not apply: no duty to report`
    ELSE IF NOT `I became aware or suspected`
         THEN `no duty to report yet: you have not become aware of, or suspected, an avoidance purpose`
         ELSE CONSIDER `s 16(3) -- what became of the notice of avoidance` `the day I became aware` `the days that were reasonably practicable` `I have notified the Authority` `the day I notified it` `today`
              WHEN `done in time` THEN `reported in time`
              WHEN `still open` THEN `not yet reported, and still in time`
              WHEN `not done in time` THEN `not reported as soon as reasonably practicable (s 16(3))`

@export Am I treated as having contravened a labour hire civil penalty provision because I was involved in someone else's contravention, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 95)? A person who aids, abets, counsels or procures, induces, is knowingly concerned in or party to, or conspires in a contravention is treated as if they had contravened the provision.
GIVEN `how I was involved` IS A `How I was involved` @desc How you were involved: you aided, abetted, counselled or procured it; you induced it, by threats, promises or otherwise; you were knowingly concerned in it or party to it, directly or indirectly; you conspired with others to contravene it; or you were not involved in any of these ways
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I treated as a contravener because I was involved` MEANS `s 95 -- treated as having contravened the provision` `how I was involved`

@export Must the labour hire provider show me its licence when I ask, as a host, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 46)? Yes: a licence holder must produce its licence for inspection when a host asks. Not doing so is an offence (up to 12 penalty units for an individual, 60 for a company).
GIVEN `I have asked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have asked the provider to produce its licence for inspection
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the provider show me its licence as a host` MEANS
    `s 46 -- the licence must be produced` (IF `I have asked` THEN `a host` ELSE `nobody has asked`)

§§ `Penalties and time limits (ss 93, 94, 97, 98)`

@export What is the most a host can be ordered to pay, in penalty units, for a contravention under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 94)? Using an unlicensed provider (s 15(1)) or entering an avoidance arrangement (s 16(2)): 800 penalty units for an individual, 3200 for a company; not reporting an avoidance arrangement (s 16(3)): 200 and 800; threats or detriment (s 86): 200 and 800. The dollar value of a penalty unit is set each year under the Monetary Units Act 2004.
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision contravened` @desc The provision: usually s 15(1) entering into an arrangement with an unlicensed provider; s 16(2) entering into an avoidance arrangement; s 16(3) not reporting an avoidance arrangement; s 86(1) threats or intimidation; s 86(2) dismissal or detriment; or another provision of the Act
      `I am a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a body corporate (answer no for an individual)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most a host can be ordered to pay` MEANS `the maximum penalty units for` `the provision` `I am a company`

@export Can a court still order me, as a host, to pay a civil (pecuniary) penalty, and which court, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (ss 93, 97, 98)? The Authority must apply within 6 years of the contravention; there is no pecuniary penalty after a conviction for substantially the same conduct, and the civil case waits while criminal proceedings go on.
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision contravened` @desc The provision said to be contravened (usually s 15(1), s 16(2) or s 16(3))
      `I am a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a body corporate (answer no for an individual)
      `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE @desc The day of the contravention (for s 15(1), the day you entered into the arrangement)
      `the day the Authority applies` IS A DATE @desc The day the Authority applied (or would apply) to the court
      `I was convicted for the same conduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted of an offence constituted by conduct substantially the same as the contravention
      `criminal proceedings are under way` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether criminal proceedings for an offence constituted by substantially the same conduct have been started against you and are not finished
GIVETH A `Whether a pecuniary penalty can be ordered`
`Can a host be ordered to pay a civil penalty` MEANS
    `Part 6 -- whether a pecuniary penalty can be ordered` `the provision` `I am a company` `the day of the contravention` `the day the Authority applies` `I was convicted for the same conduct` `criminal proceedings are under way`

@export Until what day can the Labour Hire Licensing Authority apply for a civil penalty against me for a contravention under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 93(7))? The application must be made within 6 years of the contravention.
GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE @desc The day of the contravention (for s 15(1), the day you entered into the arrangement)
GIVETH A DATE
`Until when can the Authority pursue me as a host` MEANS `s 93(7) -- the last day to apply for a pecuniary penalty` `the day of the contravention`

§§ `Helpers (not questions)`

DECLARE `Whether I had to report` IS ONE OF
    `s 16 does not apply: no duty to report`
    `no duty to report yet: you have not become aware of, or suspected, an avoidance purpose`
    `reported in time`
    `not yet reported, and still in time`
    `not reported as soon as reasonably practicable (s 16(3))`
